    fix(ci): DF-2026-13 move test-count gate to generated manifest
    
    The CI step asserting AGENTS.md test counts could never be satisfied from an
    unattended tick: AGENTS.md is a protected agent-instruction file whose write
    is refused in unattended/api_server sessions, so every commit that changed
    suite/test counts left CI red with no legitimate remediation path.
    
    The gate now reads a generated, committed, non-protected manifest:
    test-counts.json at the repo root.
    
    - scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh: sync mode (default) extracts the vitest
      totals and writes test-counts.json (never AGENTS.md); --check mode asserts
      the manifest matches the live vitest output with the same extraction
      regexes and the same GAP-032/GAP-012 error classes. CLI shape unchanged:
      `scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh [--check] [vitest-output-file]`. The
      script no longer reads or writes AGENTS.md at all (pinned by a source
      invariant test). DUCKBRAIN_COUNTS_MANIFEST env seam exists solely so the
      hermetic test can point at a temp manifest; CI never sets it.
    - .github/workflows/ci.yml: assert step renamed to "Assert test-counts.json
      matches live suite" with a comment noting why the gate moved. No other
      steps changed.
    - test-counts.json: generated from the current live suite (243 suites, 2036
      tests, which include this change's new test file — manifest and test
      addition land in the SAME commit, as the gate requires).
    - src/test/sync-agents-md-counts.test.ts: 9 hermetic tests (temp-dir
      fixtures, no network, no ports) — sync writes correct totals; --check
      exit 0 on match; sync idempotent on match; partial-failure summary parses;
      drifted manifest -> non-zero + GAP-012 drift message naming both counts;
      missing manifest -> GAP-032; unparseable vitest output -> GAP-032 in both
      modes; missing vitest file -> GAP-032; source invariant: no non-comment
      line of the script references AGENTS.md.
    - docs: the only docs/ mention of the old gate is the historical record row
      in docs/evidence/DB-GAP-065-evidence.md (evidence of a past tick's actual
      command output); deliberately left unedited — rewriting recorded evidence
      would falsify it.
    
    Evidence:
    - pnpm test:run | tee /tmp/vitest-DF-2026-13.out -> 243 passed (243) files,
      2036 passed (2036) tests, exit 0 (includes the 9 new tests).
    - bash scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh /tmp/vitest-DF-2026-13.out ->
      "test-counts.json synced to live suite: 243 suites, 2036 tests", exit 0.
    - bash scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh --check /tmp/vitest-DF-2026-13.out
      -> "test-counts.json test counts match live suite (243 suites, 2036
      tests)", exit 0.
    - Negative control: manifest hand-edited to 2035 tests -> --check exit 1
      with "GAP-012 drift: test-counts.json (243 suites, 2035 tests) != live
      (243 suites, 2036 tests)"; restored -> exit 0.
    - pnpm tsc --noEmit clean; npx prettier --check clean on touched files.
    - git diff AGENTS.md: empty (protected file untouched, as required).
    
    ch:trace row=DF-2026-13 spec=scripts/sync-agents-md-counts.sh test=src/test/sync-agents-md-counts.test.ts::sync-check-drift-rejection evidence=/tmp/vitest-DF-2026-13.out+test-counts.json witness=none:worktree-local-runs commit=THIS
    
